# Read by oxlint (not eslint 9) to prune directory traversal: the examples/*
# trees are standalone workspaces whose own .oxlintrc.json files load their own
# copy of the @nx/oxlint boundaries plugin — walking into them from the root
# workspace registers the "@nx" JS plugin twice and fails the whole run.
# Config-file ignorePatterns cannot express this: oxlint applies it after
# nested-config discovery; only CLI/ignore-file patterns prune the walk.
# ESLint 9 warns that this file is unsupported; that is expected, it is not
# ESLint's file.
/examples
